    "guidance": "Experimental/lower-priority specialist: it passed only 4/12 in-distribution runs, so do not use it as a default or as evidence that block-displacement handling works. Its dual-reference prior is intended for reliable block translation with a correct observed destination, but neither that benefit nor the clearance blend has out-of-distribution validation. If invoked, require drawer_position >0.26 and stable, reliable object_pose/height and target_pose, a low block, and an open gripper at normal entry. Avoid rotated/displaced setups that can make block-relative targets unreachable/colliding, noisy height near the blend transition, wrong destination, or uncertain grasp recovery; prefer h02 for near-nominal block plus TCP/configuration mismatch and h03 for explicit conservative low-clearance guarding. Watch for large object/destination candidate disagreement, abrupt blend-band targets, destination motion below the roof, no extraction/lift, closed fingers without coupling, drop, drawer disturbance, or IK/limit faults. In validation all eight failures kept the drawer near 0.300 and had zero IK-unconverged steps but never reached retrieval, so an open drawer and clean IK are not sufficient progress indicators. Hand off only after persistent coupling, tunnel exit, positive block-bottom clearance above 0.16 m (or already inside), drawer_position >0.26, high destination-branch weight, and destination-directed motion; blend weight or closure alone is insufficient."
